yle.** At minimum its title and end cards still show the old cat icon. `promo/icon.py` reads `docs/icon.png`, which no longer exists — render the new icon from `docs/assets/icon.svg` instead. The user uploads the final mp4 to GitHub themselves (user-attachments URL), then the site's `<source src>` and README link need the new URL."," "," **Why:** user said the video can be remade to match once the page is done.","-**How to apply:** when the page is finalized, offer the video pass; the kit is in promo/ (see promo/README.md, `promo/render.sh`). The user uploads the final mp4 to GitHub themselves (user-attachments URL).","+**How to apply:** offer the video pass when the user returns to the promo; the kit is in `promo/` (see `promo/README.md`, `promo/render.sh`), never committed."]}],"originalFile":"---\nname: site-redesign-and-video-remake\ndescription: \"skryn.app redesign (2026-09-30) — v3 \\\"Marked up\\\" chosen; promo video to be remade afterwards to match\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038\n  modified: 2026-09-30T23:27:18.802Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-09-30 three site drafts were built in docs/v1–v3 (Storyboard, Playground, Marked up); the user picked **v3 \"Marked up\"** and was iterating on it via marked-up screenshots (blue marks = their comments). A new app icon (window + red circled line + arrow + \"1\" badge on lavender wallpaper) replaced the meme cat icon in the AppIcon set and docs/assets/icon.svg.\n\nPending, in order: finish v3 → promote it to docs/index.html (paths `../assets/` → `assets/`, delete v1/v2 and the assets only they use) → then **remake the promo video \"a little bit\" to match the new style** (at minimum the title/end cards still show the old cat icon; promo/icon.py knocks a white square out of docs/icon.png, which won't fit the new icon).\n\n**Why:** user said the video can be remade to match once the page is done.\n**How to apply:** when the page is finalized, offer the video pass; the kit is in promo/ (see promo/README.md, `promo/render.sh`). The user uploads the final mp4 to GitHub themselves (user-attachments URL).\n","userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"deaf429f-ce83-4b60-9e8e-a1a80de8d4ab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","root":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":13,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"rsedykh/skryn","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"rsedykh/skryn","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"rsedykh/skryn","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"258598e8-6e4f-4097-b66f-037ec410ddc6","session_id":"71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","sessionId":"71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"main"}
